      'A powerful story asks for choices: what is the core? Which scenes carry your theme? Which conflict, longing or turning point shows who you are and how you have changed?',
      'In The Story of my Life you learn to translate your personal experience into a story that takes the reader or viewer along. Not by telling everything, but by choosing exactly those moments that give meaning to your life and touch something universal.',
    ],
    diepteTitle: 'Writing from craft and depth',
    diepte: [
      'This course combines storytelling technique with personal deepening. You learn the building blocks of a strong story and put them into practice straight away in your own text.',
      'We work with theory, writing exercises, feedback and systemic work. Along the way we also explore the family patterns, loyalties and hidden dynamics that shape your story — and the way you look at life.',
      'So you are not only working on a better manuscript, you also discover what your story truly wants to tell.',
    ],
    reisEyebrow: 'The programme',
    reisTitle: 'The journey in five weekends',
    focus: 'Focus',
    inhoud: 'Content',
    coach: 'Additional coach',
    weekends: [
      { n: 'Weekend 1', h: 'The architecture of the story', sub: 'From idea to narrative', focus: 'The foundation. The essential difference between a chronological list of events and a compelling story.', body: 'We define your central theme and select the scenes that really matter. We also look at how to position yourself as the ‘main character’ and which basic structure your story needs to truly come alive.' },
      { n: 'Weekend 2', h: 'The roots of the story', sub: 'Family, system and dynamics', focus: 'The systemic work and the invisible forces.', body: 'How do family lines shape your perspective? We explore patterns and loyalties. This weekend reveals the ‘why’ behind the events, which brings deep emotional layers into your text.', guest: 'This weekend Jessica Abicht joins as an additional coach. Jessica is an expert in family constellations.' },
      { n: 'Weekend 3', h: 'The emotional core', sub: 'Conflict, contrast and development', focus: 'The psychological engine of the story.', body: 'A story lives by conflict and growth. How do you describe the struggles, the fight, the doubt and the eventual victory? We work on the arc of your personal development, so the reader does not just observe but truly lives it with you.' },
      { n: 'Weekend 4', h: 'The senses of the story', sub: 'Sensory writing & atmosphere', focus: 'The technique of ‘showing’ instead of ‘telling’ (show, don’t tell).', body: 'How do you translate smells, sounds and textures into words? We make the scenes tangible and vivid. This is the moment your text stops being a ‘report’ and becomes an experience; we take the step towards drama the reader can feel.' },
      { n: 'Weekend 5', h: 'The finale', sub: 'Rhythm, editing and universal meaning', focus: 'Finishing and connecting with the world.', body: 'We polish the texts for a smooth rhythm and keep the thread intact. The closing focuses on universal meaning: what does your personal story say about being human?' },
    ],
    krijgTitle: 'What you receive',
    krijg: [
      { h: 'Storytelling theory', p: 'Clear insights from film and narrative writing: structure, character, conflict, scene, rhythm and theme.' },
      { h: 'Writing exercises', p: 'Practical assignments that let you work on your own text during every weekend.' },
      { h: 'Systemic insight', p: 'A deeper look at your family system, the patterns and loyalties that help shape your story.' },
      { h: 'Personal guidance', p: 'Individual feedback on your progress, in writing and online, between the weekends.' },
      { h: 'Group dynamics', p: 'Inspiration, recognition and engaged feedback in a small, safe group.' },
    ],
    quote: 'The strength of The Story of my Life lies in the combination of craft, personal deepening and consistent practice. You not only learn how a story works, you also develop the courage and clarity to truly write your own.',
    gertEyebrow: 'Your guide',
    gertName: 'Gert Embrechts',
    gertRole: 'Coach, storyteller and creative facilitator',
    gert: [
      'Gert Embrechts worked for more than thirty years in film as a screenwriter, director and creative producer. For many years he taught at film schools at home and abroad and guided makers in developing their own voice, vision and creative power.',
      'Today Gert also works as a coach for individuals, couples and groups, focusing on awareness, communication and the often invisible patterns that connect people — or create distance between them.',
      'His approach is shaped by a powerful combination of storytelling, teaching and personal development. Just as every story is driven by underlying motives, roles and conflicts, relationships too are shaped by old beliefs, family dynamics and recurring patterns.',
    ],
    gertLink: 'About Jessica and Gert',
    voorTitle: 'Who is this course for?',
    voor: [
      'People who want to write their life story, family history or personal experiences',
      'Beginning writers who want to develop more technique, structure and confidence',
      'People working on a book, novel, memoir or screenplay',
      'Writers who want to give their text more emotional depth and expressive power',
      'Anyone who loves to write and wants to go deeper into storytelling',
    ],
    locEyebrow: 'The location',
    locTitle: 'Room to listen',
    loc: [
      'The course takes place at Homecoming Land in Brasschaat: a 2.5-hectare woodland estate with several serene spots to write, slow down and connect with your own story.',
      'The natural surroundings offer peace, space and silence — exactly what is needed to listen to what wants to be written.',
    ],
    locLink: 'Location & directions',
    prakEyebrow: 'All-in programme',
    prakTitle: 'Practical information',
    prak: [
      { h: 'Duration', p: '5 weekends, spread over 9 months' },
      { h: 'Dates (subject to change)', list: ['24–25 April 2027', '26–27 June 2027', '11–12 September 2027', '30–31 October 2027', '15–16 January 2028'] },
      { h: 'Group size', p: 'Maximum 12 participants' },
      { h: 'Guidance', p: '70 hours of live teaching, 4 written feedback rounds and 4 individual online feedback sessions' },
      { h: 'Included', p: 'Meals during the 10 course days' },
      { h: 'Accommodation', p: 'Discount available at Hotel Van der Valk – Dennenhof, across the road from Homecoming Land' },
      { h: 'Payment', p: 'Online via iDEAL, Bancontact or card. Payment in instalments possible' },
    ],
    priceLabel: 'Contribution',
    price: '€ 2,450',
    stapTitle: 'Choose your next step',
    stappen: [
      { value: 'inschrijving', h: 'Register', p: 'Give your story the structure, depth and shape it deserves — with guidance, attention and room to truly write.' },
      { value: 'kennismaking', h: 'Book an introductory call', p: 'Would you like to feel first whether this course suits you and your writing project? Book a no-obligation conversation.' },
    ],
    formChoice: 'What would you like to do?',
    formProject: 'Tell us a little about your writing project (optional)',
    formConsent: 'I agree that my details are used to handle my request.',
    formSubmit: 'Send',
    formNote: 'You will soon receive a reply with all practical information.',
    payTitle: 'Paying your contribution',
    pay: 'Registered? Then you can pay your contribution securely online right away. Prefer to pay in instalments? Mention it in the form and we will send you a payment plan.',
    payBtn: 'Pay online',
    payMethods: 'iDEAL · Bancontact · card · secure via Mollie',
    closing: 'Your life is unique. Give the story that lives in you the shape to touch others.',
    alt: { gert: 'Gert Embrechts', hero: 'Morning light falling across a woodland path at Homecoming Land', loc: 'The garden at Homecoming Land under a cloudy sky' },
